From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000085 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: fix AW9523 parent EINT

The MT6797 parent interrupt domain consumes raw EINT channel numbers, not
physical GPIO numbers.  The recovered non-linear map assigns the AW9523
interrupt on GPIO87 to EINT10, but the disabled board candidate currently
specifies EINT87.

Use the correct EINT10 parent interrupt.  Keep the bus, expander and matrix
consumer disabled.  This fixes the declarative resource without claiming
that the parent interrupt path works on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@ aw9523: gpio-expander@5b {
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&keyboard_soc_pins>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
-		interrupts = <87 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		interrupts = <10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		gpio-controller;
 		#gpio-cells = <2>;
 		gpio-ranges = <&aw9523 0 0 16>;
-- 
